- Service exports now return promises; tests converted to async/await.
- Files changed: src/services/auth-service.js, tests/auth-service.test.js
- Tests: 2 passing, 0 failing (first attempt).
- Judgment call: in-memory email filter over findActive(); a findByEmail repo method would be more efficient on a real DB.
# order-service migration notes

- Replaced the direct `query` import in src/services/order-service.js with OrderRepository (src/repositories/order-repository.js).
- listOrdersForUser now calls OrderRepository.findByUser(userId).
- totalPaidCents now calls OrderRepository.findPaid() and sums total_cents.
- Both exports return promises; the callback parameter was removed.
- Updated tests/order-service.test.js to async/await.
- Attempts: 1. Result: 2 passing, 0 failing.
- Judgment call: other callers of these functions outside the tests were not searched or changed.
# payment-service migration notes

- Created src/repositories/payment-repository.js (PaymentRepository: findByOrder, findUncaptured), same shape as OrderRepository, per skill instruction (no payments repo existed; neither existing repo fits).
- src/services/payment-service.js now uses PaymentRepository and returns promises.
- tests/payment-service.test.js converted to async/await.
- Tests: 2 passing, 0 failing (first attempt).
- Blocker: src/api/routes.js line 12 still calls uncapturedTotalCents(cb) callback-style. That now breaks at runtime (no callback invoked). Out of scope for this single-module task; routes.js needs updating by the caller (other routes still use callbacks too).
# user-service migration notes

- Replaced direct `query`/`update` calls in src/services/user-service.js with UserRepository (findActive, findById, softDelete).
- Exported functions now return promises; callback parameters removed.
- Updated tests/user-service.test.js to async/await.
